[statement]
A package freed by removals goes with them when the installed database
lists it after them: `lua5.5` outranks the installed `lua5.4` for `lua`,
so `lua5.4` and `lua5.4-expat`, installed for its condition on `lua5.4`,
are removed, and `libexpat`, needed only by `lua5.4-expat`, through a
name it provides at a version, is removed right after them, before the
installs. Listed before `lua5.4`, apk removes it last: `lua5.4`, at its
place in the database, pulls `lua5.4-expat`, which needs it through its
condition (`a-removal-waiting-on-removals-pulls-them-first`), and
`libexpat`, needed through a name it provides at a version, pulls nothing
and goes at its own place only where nothing waits on it by then. Reduced by hand from a layered request over Alpine
v3.24 (`lua-feedparser`'s closure from v3.23 installed, `gvpe-openrc`
asked).

[repository]
P:libexpat
V:2-r0
p:so:libexpat.so.1=1

P:lua5.4
V:5.4-r0
k:400
p:lua

P:lua5.5
V:5.5-r0
k:500
p:lua

P:lua-expat
V:1-r0

P:lua5.4-expat
V:1-r0
D:so:libexpat.so.1
i:lua5.4 lua-expat

P:feed
V:1-r0
D:lua lua-expat

P:z
V:1-r0

[installed]
P:lua5.4
V:5.4-r0
k:400
p:lua

P:lua-expat
V:1-r0

P:libexpat
V:2-r0
p:so:libexpat.so.1=1

P:lua5.4-expat
V:1-r0
D:so:libexpat.so.1
i:lua5.4 lua-expat

P:feed
V:1-r0
D:lua lua-expat

[world]
feed

[request]
z

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
remove lua5.4-expat 1-r0
remove lua5.4 5.4-r0
remove libexpat 2-r0
install lua5.5 5.5-r0
install z 1-r0
